1
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,121
I cut my arm. Look at it.

2
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:28,129
- It's not healing.
- Do you mean...?

3
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,651
I'm staying hurt.

4
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,411
Don't you see?
The whole world becomes immortal.

5
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:36,366
And I'm mortal. I don't mend.
I'm normal again.

6
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:39,723
This, Captain, fascinates me.

7
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:44,050
- What makes you so different?
- I don't know.

8
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:47,881
And yet you're the only one left,
the only true human. So tell me,

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,129
what did you give them so long ago?

10
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,730
Why would he want you dead?

11
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:56,367
On the very day that no-one's dying?
Wish I knew.

12
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:59,290
Every time you turn up,
it always go wrong.

13
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,004
Where are you from?

14
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:04,681
Long ago and so far away.

15
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:16,649
MAN: Harkness. Anyone?

16
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,603
Jack Harkness.

17
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:21,041
I'm looking for Jack Harkness.

18
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,730
That's me.

19
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,961
Welcome to America, Mr Harkness.

20
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,844
There's your visa all stamped.

21
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:31,008
Grazie. I mean,
thank you very much, Inspector.

22
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,929
Hey, wait! Stop that man!

23
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,606
Come on now.

24
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,402
You're not Jack Harkness.
The visa's mine.

25
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:52,760
It's what?

26
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,609
You'll find everything's in order.

27
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,564
The British consulate arranged for my
travel through the embassy in Rome.

28
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,045
That visa belongs to me.

29
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:02,970
Yes, sir.
Terribly sorry this happened, sir.

30
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:07,923
Take him away. Send him back home.

31
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:11,288
- There you are.
- Thank you.

32
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:29,090
You're still here.
I thought you'd be in the city by now.

33
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,009
Time to spare.

34
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,929
Waiting for the next boat to Manhattan.

35
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:36,089
I also am waiting for a boat.
Mine goes all the way

36
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,850
- back to Italy.
- Right.

37
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:40,042
That's what they do with thieves.

38
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:48,689
An interesting fact is they do it
also with people who forge visas.

39
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,285
Good eye.

40
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,448
- Why didn't you tell them?
- I wasn't sure.

41
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:04,281
Until that moment when you said,
"Why didn't you tell them?"

42
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:08,803
I'm on a kind of unofficial
official visit,

43
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,890
one part of the government
pretending to be another part.

44
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,485
You work for a government?

45
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:18,002
Look at me.
Do I look like a bureaucrat?

46
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,328
Never seen a man like you before.

47
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,124
More like a soldier.

48
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,847
Your English is good. Where did you learn?

49
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,611
We had a schoolmaster in the village.

50
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,643
He taught me.

51
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:37,209
I went to him every single day
because I always dreamt of coming here.

52
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,322
- What's the village?
- You wouldn't know it.

53
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:41,010
No-one ever does.

54
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,770
Tiny place on the Amalfi Coast.

55
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:46,248
And I mean, for certain,
right on the coast.

56
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:50,206
The whole place is holding its breath
on the edge of a cliff top.

57
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:53,369
If you look over,
hundreds of feet down to the sea.

58
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:56,643
Sounds beautiful. Why'd you ever leave?

59
00:03:56,760 --> 00:04:01,084
New York. They have buildings here
taller than the cliff.

60
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,486
- I wanted to see that.
- You wait.

61
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,887
They've only just started building.

62
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,606
Years to come, they're going to have...

63
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:11,645
- What? They're going to have what?
- Never mind. What's your name?

64
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:13,888
Angelo Colasanto.

65
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:17,566
Angelo Colasanto.

66
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,646
- La magia oscura!
- It's not magic.

67
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:30,082
Technology.
Sometimes they're indistinguishable.

68
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:32,486
Hey, hey, he!!!

69
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:35,001
How does it work? Can I see it?

70
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,482
Hey, over here!

71
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,602
We just found this man's papers.

72
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,165
You can let him go.

73
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:46,408
We're going to Manhattan.

74
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,166
Who are you?

75
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:23,851
What do you want?

76
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,724
What do you want?!

77
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,365
Rhys, call me, OK?

78
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:49,845
Mam, if you can, call me, OK?

79
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:02,002
Vera! Vera! Vera!

80
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:07,644
How many views have we got now?

81
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,922
Um, over five million.

82
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:16,204
People are setting up
memorial services for her too.

83
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:19,688
Just random people
who didn't even know her.

84
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:22,167
I just, urn...

85
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,401
You got the footage

86
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,284
and that's going to make the difference.

87
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,289
But I've been meaning to say, I...

88
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,768
I know that that must have been...

89
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,000
I'm sorry.

90
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,041
I got ya.

91
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:39,606
No, really, Rex.

92
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:43,929
I really didn't even know her
that well, OK?

93
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,929
- But you did. You must have talked.
- Look, she...

94
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,930
she told me about her mother,
her ex-husband,

95
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:51,611
possibly something about
a brother or a sister.

96
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,688
I don't know, maybe not.

97
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,683
- The obituary says...
- Yeah. But what does it matter?

98
00:06:56,800 --> 00:07:00,009
Hmm? Whoever she was, it's gone.

99
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:03,203
- I don't even know where she's from.
- The news is saying San Antonio.

100
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,448
Well, then, go Spurs!

101
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,685
Sorry.

102
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,571
I don't know how to help.

103
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:15,526
Except that...maybe her death
has changed things.

104
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:17,688
They'll shut down the camps.

105
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:22,169
No, they "paused" the camps.
That's all they're saying. Paused.

106
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:25,011
And while the politicians
are all denying everything,

107
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,964
those ovens are still out there,
waiting to burn.

108
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,162
-
-Jack!

109
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,169
- Gwen, you're back.
- Where's Jack?

110
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,441
Sorry about your dad.

111
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,085
- Did you hear any news?
- No, not really.

112
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,770
- Jack!
- He went outside.

113
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,609
Jack?
Hey!

114
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,290
I missed you.

115
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:42,482
I've been searching
through that Blessing stuff.

116
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:45,524
Listen, you've got to come down to
the car. I've got to show you something.

117
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:48,246
- Anything good?
- No, just stuff from back home.

118
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:50,442
Souvenir sort of thing.
just you and me. Come on.

119
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:53,211
All right, stop your nagging.
Told you she missed me

120
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,083
GWEN: Yeah, today would be good, Jack.

121
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:59,170
-
- Bad day, Gwen?

122
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:04,169
Ohh!

123
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:12,202
All right. OK.

124
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:41,086
I'm sorry. My Italian isn't so...

125
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:43,851
She's saying there is only one bed.

126
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:46,281
-
- Ah!

127
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:49,210
- I said I'll sleep on the floor.
- On the floor, yes.

128
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,891
He'll sleep on the floor.

129
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:00,085
Come-a down to the shop any time.

130
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:03,044
Family butcher's is fine food.

131
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:04,400
And you are family now.

132
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:17,044
It's a good room.

133
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,970
And it's cheap.

134
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,362
You should save your money,
Angelo Colasanto.

135
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,609
Next couple of years,
earn as much as you can.

136
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:29,563
Save it all up

137
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:32,968
cos you're going to need it.
Bad times ahead.

138
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,883
Why, what's going to happen?

139
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,844
Oh! Oh, so many things.

140
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:41,247
Don't worry. It gets better.

141
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,490
Then it gets worse again.

142
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:46,125
You talk funny.

143
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:48,720
I'm a very funny man.

144
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:56,245
Scars.

145
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:58,010
You been in a lot of fights?

146
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:01,806
Sometimes you have to defend yourself,
you know?

147
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:09,808
RADIO: Another non-stop hour
of music, weather...

148
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:14,205
...and allegations continue to surface

149
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,687
about procedures
at the new medical facilities.

150
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:19,883
But Oswald Danes has released
a statement in which he says

151
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,731
that a global emergency
calls for emergency measures

152
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:26,208
and he advocated a swift return
to the category policy.

153
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,850
Ah! I'm tied down.

154
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:31,689
- Why am I tied down?
- They're in my eyes.

155
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:33,689
- What?
- They're in my eyes.

156
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:34,847
The contacts. They're in my eyes.

157
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,531
Somebody's taken Anwen, Rhys,
my mother, the whole bloody family,

158
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:39,449
and they've said if I bring you,
they'll let them go unharmed.

159
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:43,086
Don't try moving.
You'll never get out of those knots.

160
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:47,086
My... My hands are asleep.

161
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,810
And my feet. You tied my feet?!

162
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:52,002
Of course I did, stupid.
Otherwise you'd get out of the car,

163
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:53,326
knock me out and turn the car around.

164
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:58,290
- Are you sure they have your family?
- I phoned 100 times.

165
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:01,802
There's no reply.
They... They've got them.

166
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:05,003
I want to talk to the lenses.
Look at me so I can talk to them.

167
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:07,600
Why do you always keep thinking
you can tell me what to do?

168
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:11,566
Pull over or look into the rear-view.
just, please, let me talk to them.

169
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:14,689
Don't cock this up, OK?

170
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:20,808
Listen, whoever you are,
there's more than one way to play this.

171
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,166
Are you listening?

172
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:25,044
Yeah, there's a cursor. They're there.

173
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:26,889
You want me?

174
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,288
Let her family go
and I'll come to you alone.

175
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:33,244
- Tell them they can have me too.
- No, just me.

176
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:37,684
Let Rhys go, let Anwen go,
let her mother go free.

177
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:41,361
You guys, you know what?
Here I am. You got me.

178
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:43,323
GWEN: Nothing.

179
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,885
- Give them a minute.
- There's just nothing now.

180
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,287
- Maybe they're thinking about it.
- My mother's name is Mary.

181
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:48,561
Mary!

182
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,081
You've known me all this time
and you can't remember her name?

183
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:53,202
- All right, I'm sorry, OK?
- Yeah. Well, you should be,

184
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,401
because this is all your fault.

185
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:57,444
They want to kill you,
but why do they want to do that?

186
00:11:57,560 --> 00:12:00,006
- I don't know.
- What have you done?

187
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,121
I don't know!

188
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,844
Well, you've done something,
haven't you?

189
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,689
Way back when
in that long bloody life of yours.

190
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:07,201
God, you've lived so long, you can't
remember half of it. Now you think.

191
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:09,971
Think! What the hell have you done?

192
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,569
JACK: I love this. I love weddings.

193
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:19,045
I don't believe in marriage.

194
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:21,288
So young, so handsome and so cynical.

195
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,201
ANGELO: Look at them.

196
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:27,206
What are their chances?

197
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:30,324
That's what makes it
so brave and wonderful...

198
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,601
making a promise and going forward.

199
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:34,326
It doesn't matter
what happens in the future.

200
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:37,887
Right now, it's real
and it happens and it's true.

201
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,041
You're Catholic, right?

202
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:45,965
Do you want to kneel down like that?

203
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,242
He doesn't hear me.

204
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:50,886
He doesn't hear you? Why?

205
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,371
You know why.

206
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:59,490
That's our padre. Wait here.

207
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:06,124
Forgive me, Father, for I have sinned...
so many times,

208
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:08,208
and that's just today.

209
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:15,163
It's been about...700 years
since my last confession.

210
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:17,761
Where do I start?

211
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,286
How about the triplets?

212
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:23,084
Or the naked circus?

213
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:26,249
Or that Sapphic leapfrog jamboree?

214
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:31,811
No.

215
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:38,491
Let's just start with the sin of...
"Father Timothy sent me."

216
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,486
- You're Jack Harkness?
- Good to see you, Father.

217
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:48,206
I believe we're going to talk business.

218
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:51,847
The Volstead Act makes an exception
for sacramental wines.

219
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:54,691
And the brothers upstate
produce more than we can use.

220
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:58,885
The extra income feeds
a lot of widows and orphans, I'm sure.

221
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:03,449
Yes, I'm doing this entirely
for charity, every last cent.

222
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:05,050
It's not very good.

223
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:07,731
It's the blood of Christ, Angelo.
I'm sure it's good enough.

224
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,410
This is just a sample.

225
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:12,251
If you make enough profit,
we'll start delivering crates.

226
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:14,488
We should figure out a system.

227
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:17,683
Hey, what are you doing?
Who are you?

228
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:19,768
It's OK.
Let them take us, Angelo. It's OK.

229
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,291
Where are they taking us?

230
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:25,367
I don't know where. just east.

231
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,362
Did they say get on the 10 going east?

232
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:31,609
Or on the eastbound 10 Freeway,
or what?

233
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:34,530
If they said highway,
they could be from back east.

234
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:36,051
If their grammar was wrong,

235
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:37,605
it could mean that English
is not their first language.

236
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:39,643
- I didn't notice anything wrong with it.
- You're Welsh.

237
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:40,841
You wouldn't notice
if the vowels were missing.

238
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,200
Button it!

239
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:48,121
Hey, you've got a gun, haven't you?

240
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,924
- You could smuggle it back here to me.
- It's gone.

241
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:51,166
They made me leave it behind.

242
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,566
Just give it up, Jack,
with all this planning, OK?

243
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:54,045
Because if there was a way out of this,

244
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,481
I can guarantee you
I would have thought of it.

245
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:04,601
Gwen, I shouldn't... There are reasons
I shouldn't even say this...

246
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:06,370
secrets...

247
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,323
but we could...we could find Anwen.

248
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:11,369
My wrist strap, it could find her.

249
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:13,601
We could save her.

250
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:16,201
What?

251
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:18,527
It's coded to my DNA.

252
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:21,325
And it resonates
to anything close to my DNA.

253
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:23,522
If you are using my daughter
as leverage, I swear to God,

254
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,051
- I will kill you myself.
- Listen to me.

255
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:29,085
If we recode it to your DNA,
then Anwen is a close match.

256
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,931
It would respond to her.
Like a tracker.

257
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:35,601
We could save her together.
We could rescue her.

258
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:38,200
You could do that?
You could do that recode thing?

259
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:42,962
Yes. A drop of your blood. A single cell
would do, but a drop would be easier.

260
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,081
- Let's do it.
- Pull over.

261
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,690
OK, let's do it. I'll have to untie you.

262
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,361
One hand for just a second,
all right, Gwen?

263
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:51,925
I'd be saving Anwen.

264
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:02,766
You bastard.

265
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,047
Nice try.

266
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,362
GWEN: Oh, mm-hmm.

267
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:16,041
Whoever this is...they know you.

268
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,844
Phew!

269
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:26,490
So, Mr Harkness...and his acolyte.

270
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:28,807
- Yeah, and who are you?
- Your friend thinks he's funny.

271
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:32,163
He doesn't. He isn't. He's sorry.
This is Sal Maranzano.

272
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:34,806
- You were going to undercut my price.
- We found some untapped resource.

273
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:37,685
Rumour is you two are a pair of finocchi.

274
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,770
That's not a rumour. That's a boast.

275
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:45,851
And if you were really upset about
some small-time competition,

276
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,610
it'd already be hailing bullets.

277
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:49,404
So we're here for another reason.

278
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:52,410
I don't think so. Take 'em, kill 'em.

279
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:54,010
Give us a try, Maranzano.

280
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:57,283
You need men like us, off the grid.

281
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:59,368
Men who could never
be traced back to you.

282
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:02,563
So whatever it is you need, Sal,
no matter how dangerous it is,

283
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:04,250
no matter how strange it is,

284
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:06,647
you just found the right men.

285
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:12,168
There's a box in a warehouse

286
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,851
that needs to find its way
to another warehouse.

287
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:16,485
You can count on us.

288
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:20,088
You will not look in the box.

289
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,486
Sure thing.

290
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:29,001
You will swear...
on everything that is holy

291
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:33,091
you will deliver the box,
but you will not look inside.

292
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,485
I promise.

293
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,200
Then we got a deal.

294
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:47,244
Tomorrow night, Gallaco Wharf, Bay Five.

295
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:51,489
Get going. Get lost.

296
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,521
- You're running away?
- No.

297
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:02,728
That's mine! Wh...

298
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:03,762
What are you doing?

299
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,211
You're packing my things!

300
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:08,641
You need to go now. There's a plan.

301
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:09,966
And I'm not part of your plan?

302
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:12,447
Look at your hands. Not a scar on them.

303
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,324
I'm tougher than you.

304
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,681
Maranzano's people
have stumbled across something

305
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:20,565
they're not supposed to have.
I've got to stop them.

306
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,931
You made this happen?

307
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,686
You've planned this.

308
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:29,849
Since when?
Since you got on the boat to America?

309
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:32,327
Just get out of town, Angelo.
These people are bad.

310
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,646
You don't want to be on their list.

311
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,489
- Get far away.
- Who are you doing this for?

312
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:39,730
The government in England?
Or the other thing you said...Torchwood?

313
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:41,365
For the train. Go to the West Coast.

314
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,687
You're handsome enough.
Get into the movies.

315
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,564
- I'm not letting you send me away.
- Why?

316
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:47,125
Because you wouldn't know
how to get another man?

317
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:48,730
Because you're not brave enough?

318
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,365
You think I'm with you because it's easy?

319
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:52,608
- It's not easy, trust me.
- I know.

320
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:55,485
I hear the beads clicking
at night, Angelo.

321
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:58,843
Everything we do,
you ask for forgiveness afterwards.

322
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,088
That's just sex. Imagine if it was love.

323
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:04,647
What would he say then, your God?
What would he say if two men could love?

324
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:07,843
Oh! Oh, but no. No, that's impossible.

325
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:10,850
And if it's impossible,
then you can't stay with me.

326
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:11,961
You...

327
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,081
...you're an ass.

328
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:18,130
For a man who knows a lot of things,
huh, you're not so bright.

329
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,730
Think about it.

330
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:22,650
I grew up in a village with 200 people.

331
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,046
Only 200.

332
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:28,165
The sun would rise and the sun would set
over the same 200 people.

333
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:31,891
And that was it. That was my world.

334
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,525
And look at me now.

335
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:38,885
I'm a bootlegger in New York City
with you in my bed.

336
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:41,451
You think any of your little secrets

337
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,528
can change my life
more than it's already changed?

338
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,483
And yes, I...

339
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:47,887
I feel guilty about what we do.

340
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,368
It hasn't made me stop doing it.

341
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:15,086
Besides, I always hoped...

342
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,205
...if God is love,

343
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:21,448
maybe...

344
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:22,800
he loves me too.

345
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,524
That's blasphemy.

346
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,563
I think that's Christianity.

347
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:50,210
You're unpacking my things?

348
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:52,566
I've got this friend.

349
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:56,562
He's called The Doctor.

350
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:59,126
He explores the world...

351
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,570
...with a companion.

352
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:07,686
It looks nice.

353
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:13,045
Are you saying that I can stay?

354
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:16,651
Maybe.

355
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:45,971
Oh, Dio.

356
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:47,809
What's all this?

357
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:50,400
Ammonia refrigeration. Of course!

358
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:52,522
The best they could do in 1927.

359
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,724
They said, "Don't look in the box."

360
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:58,286
- Yeah, right
- What is it? What's inside?

361
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,561
Someone...

362
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:03,526
Someone way above Maranzano,
they found something, a weapon.

363
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:06,246
They told Maranzano to hold it

364
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:08,522
until after the next state election,
then ship it to Albany.

365
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:12,201
Maranzano doesn't know what he's got,
but he's terrified of it.

366
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,525
Can't say I blame him.

367
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:20,450
No. No, that's...

368
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:21,686
What?

369
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:26,442
Er, it's a parasite. Like a bug.

370
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:28,369
A parasite?

371
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,851
Tell me more about it.

372
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:33,487
Good man.

373
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:35,682
It's a species of brainspawn

374
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:39,600
treated as vermin on more than
150 planets that I know of.

375
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:42,451
And valued as dinner on one other.

376
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,251
It tastes like oysters.

377
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:48,045
- You did not.
- I had to be polite.

378
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:53,125
Now this part drills
into the brain of the host

379
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:55,641
and deposits its larvae there...

380
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:57,683
little worms,

381
00:22:57,800 --> 00:23:02,089
sharp as needles,
pushing into the brain very slowly.

382
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:05,283
You go insane, but it takes years.

383
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:06,890
Franklin Roosevelt,

384
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:10,129
he's going to be elected governor
of New York this November.

385
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:12,686
But he wouldn't start making
the really crazy decisions

386
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:14,564
until his second term as president.

387
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:19,720
Result - America destabilises,
pulls out of the war, Germany rises,

388
00:23:19,840 --> 00:23:24,084
the Third Reich triumphant, and there's
a whole new history sprawling out.

389
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:26,123
You mean someone is changing the future?

390
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:27,924
Destroying it.

391
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:31,010
Turning order into chaos
and feeding off the results.

392
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:34,761
Who would do such a thing?
These people above Maranzano.

393
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:38,441
They're just being used by someone
called The Trickster's Brigade.

394
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:40,927
Believe me, you don't wanna meet them.

395
00:23:41,040 --> 00:23:42,804
What sort of men are they?

396
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:44,285
They're not men at all.

397
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:47,205
They're not even human.

398
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:50,767
OK. OK.

399
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:54,243
Ah, he likes you.

400
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:56,886
But it's cold, yeah? So it's safe?

401
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,206
-
- Oh, Dio!

402
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,286
Ha!

403
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:06,485
That'll dissolve it.

404
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:09,562
Ah!

405
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:12,684
So...the mission is complete.

406
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:14,370
We just saved the world, Angelo.

407
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:18,804
- And no-one will ever know.
- Then, did I pass?

408
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:21,605
Can I stay with you like The Doctor?

409
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:23,370
Learn all the secrets?

410
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:25,164
-
- Here's one of the secrets...

411
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:26,327
"In!

412
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:39,605
Quick. Come on, up. Let's go!

413
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:41,848
Hold it! Stop right there!

414
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:43,610
Take my hand.

415
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:44,767
Ah!

416
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:48,161
- Grab my hand!
-

417
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:49,691
-
- No!

418
00:25:20,080 --> 00:25:21,923
All right, get him in there.

419
00:25:22,040 --> 00:25:23,565
Go! Get him up the stairs. Step up.

420
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:24,920
Jack.

421
00:25:27,840 --> 00:25:30,207
Meat cart's on the way for the other one.

422
00:25:30,320 --> 00:25:32,846
You'd better take the main gate.
Off you go.

423
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:09,366
It's me.

424
00:26:09,480 --> 00:26:12,006
- What do you mean?
- Well, it's me.

425
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:13,246
I caused this.

426
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:15,488
I made this...happen.

427
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:19,287
I knew Torchwood was toxic...

428
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:22,927
right from the moment I joined up,
the very first day, but...

429
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:24,530
I stayed.

430
00:26:28,080 --> 00:26:30,560
- I'm glad you did.
- Hah! Stop being so nice.

431
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:34,361
We left nice behind 100 miles back.

432
00:26:34,480 --> 00:26:35,811
I'm trying to be honest, OK?

433
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:39,402
Because do you know what
the worst thing is of all?

434
00:26:39,520 --> 00:26:42,763
Out of all the shit we have seen,
all the bloodshed,

435
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:46,407
all the horror, do you know
what is worse than all of that?

436
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,525
I loved it.

437
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:57,684
I bloody loved it.

438
00:26:57,800 --> 00:27:00,849
And I'd keep telling Rhys I was sorry

439
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:04,726
and I'd say to little Anwen, "I'm sorry,"
but I loved it so much.

440
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:10,924
I knew things no-one else knew
and, oh, I felt so special.

441
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:16,408
And when we lost people,
it was so, so big

442
00:27:16,520 --> 00:27:21,287
and I could say it was worth it,
because the bigger it was,

443
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:23,164
the more important I was.

444
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:24,520
And the more people we lost...

445
00:27:26,040 --> 00:27:28,611
...the more that meant I was a survivor
and I was better than them.

446
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:29,721
My God, this is all my fault.

447
00:27:29,840 --> 00:27:31,490
And now they've got
my beautiful little girl

448
00:27:31,600 --> 00:27:33,807
and I've wished this on her.

449
00:27:33,920 --> 00:27:36,287
I used to think the same
about Torchwood...

450
00:27:36,400 --> 00:27:38,562
That's what I'm saying.
Have you got what I'm saying to you, Jack?

451
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:41,001
What I'm saying is, no more.

452
00:27:42,680 --> 00:27:44,762
Cos I know exactly what you're thinking,
Jack Harkness. I know it.

453
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:46,291
"She won't do this.

454
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:48,129
"Not really. Not my Gwen.

455
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:49,924
"No, Gwen, she can't hurt me.

456
00:27:50,040 --> 00:27:52,611
"Gwen loves me.
She'd never hand me in."

457
00:27:52,720 --> 00:27:54,449
Well, this is about my daughter.

458
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:59,287
And I swear, for her sake,
I will see you killed like a dog

459
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:03,007
right in front of me if it means
her back in my arms. Understood?

460
00:28:03,120 --> 00:28:04,167
Understood.

461
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:08,165
And let me tell you,

462
00:28:08,280 --> 00:28:10,601
now that I'm mortal,

463
00:28:10,720 --> 00:28:12,802
I'm going to hang on to this
with everything I've got.

464
00:28:13,840 --> 00:28:16,764
I love you, Gwen Cooper,
but I will rip your skin from your skull

465
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:19,360
before I let you take this away from me.

466
00:28:19,480 --> 00:28:21,164
Understood?

467
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:22,645
Understood.

468
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:33,724
I feel like I know you now
better than I've ever done before.

469
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:38,606
Yeah.

470
00:28:40,520 --> 00:28:42,443
- Right at the end.
- Mmm.

471
00:28:44,720 --> 00:28:45,767
Right at the end.

472
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:57,051
Nice suit.

473
00:29:00,520 --> 00:29:02,363
Look, it's all right. Don't panic.

474
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:06,325
- It's me. I'm the same man.
- I saw you.

475
00:29:06,440 --> 00:29:07,885
I saw you get shot.

476
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:11,083
- I got better.
- You got shot in the head.

477
00:29:12,120 --> 00:29:14,600
I saw it. I saw the blood, I...

478
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:15,926
I saw your body.

479
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:20,488
- Want to see it again?
- Shut up, Jack!

480
00:29:23,560 --> 00:29:25,528
This is so wrong.

481
00:29:29,840 --> 00:29:32,650
Tell me...what happened.

482
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:36,121
You were dead.

483
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:37,924
Clearly, I wasn't.

484
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:40,047
I was playing dead.

485
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:42,322
Then I cleared out.

486
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:46,081
- I went to Los Angeles.
- No, I saw you dead.

487
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:47,884
But I'm alive.

488
00:29:51,320 --> 00:29:52,321
Feel.

489
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:54,647
You wanted to learn the secrets?

490
00:29:56,200 --> 00:29:58,567
This is the best secret of all.

491
00:29:59,640 --> 00:30:01,483
You're alive.

492
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:06,165
I'm alive.

493
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:11,447
I came back, Angelo.

494
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:15,087
I came back for you. Believe me,
I have never done that before.

495
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:18,283
I... I even got us that same old room.

496
00:30:20,040 --> 00:30:21,724
You came back for me?

497
00:30:21,840 --> 00:30:24,286
Yes. Yes, I did.

498
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:29,006
You don't know whether to hit me
or to kiss me, do you?

499
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:30,929
Come on,

500
00:30:31,040 --> 00:30:32,804
you can try both.

501
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:39,841
No scars.

502
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:41,724
You keep learning.

503
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:45,881
No.

504
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:48,446
I don't know what you are.

505
00:30:50,200 --> 00:30:51,531
I'm Jack.

506
00:30:52,800 --> 00:30:54,040
That's not the answer.

507
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:56,845
It's an answer.

508
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:57,961
First of many.

509
00:30:59,080 --> 00:31:00,081
Come on.

510
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:03,202
You've been locked away for a year.

511
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:06,405
I know you'll like this.

512
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:10,646
I can feel that you'll like this.

513
00:31:18,360 --> 00:31:20,886
- Grab my hand! No!
- Ah!

514
00:31:32,720 --> 00:31:33,767
What the hell, Angelo?

515
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:36,365
What did you do?

516
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:38,164
Il diavolo!

517
00:31:38,280 --> 00:31:39,964
I am not the devil.

518
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:43,402
It's the only way.
The devil seduces with confidence.

519
00:31:43,520 --> 00:31:47,002
No. No!

520
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:52,241
- Stay away from me, devil!
- Ah!

521
00:31:52,360 --> 00:31:54,408
Ah! God!

522
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:20,770
- Il diavolo! Il diavolo!
-Jack...

523
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:22,325
Il diavolo!

524
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:23,566
Ah!

525
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:30,883
I don't understand. Angelo,
I don't understand. What did he do?

526
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:33,241
- We can show you.
- E un miracolo.

527
00:32:33,360 --> 00:32:34,566
A miracle?

528
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:39,163
I want to see. Do it again.

529
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:50,211
JACK: No.

530
00:32:51,520 --> 00:32:52,442
No.

531
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:11,607
-
- Diavolo!

532
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:14,200
Angelo...

533
00:33:14,320 --> 00:33:15,765
Angelo!

534
00:33:17,280 --> 00:33:18,566
DOITt go!

535
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:42,051
MAN: I don't know.

536
00:33:44,560 --> 00:33:46,130
I just don't know what it is.

537
00:33:46,240 --> 00:33:49,767
Hmm. How much is the butcher asking?

538
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:55,364
10,000. Not too much for something
with so much potential.

539
00:33:55,480 --> 00:33:58,324
And we'd own him...together?

540
00:33:59,760 --> 00:34:02,604
A partnership. What do you say?

541
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:08,367
Ag reed.

542
00:34:09,880 --> 00:34:13,248
Ag reed.

543
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:28,281
This is it.

544
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:31,490
It's been a long time coming.

545
00:34:33,120 --> 00:34:34,724
All those years.

546
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:39,288
What's the most beautiful thing
you've ever seen? Not just on Earth.

547
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:41,971
I'm not doing this,
I'm not giving final speeches.

548
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,764
Just tell me,
anywhere in the universe.

549
00:34:50,760 --> 00:34:52,205
I saw a firebird once,

550
00:34:52,320 --> 00:34:54,004
a tiny little thing,

551
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:55,485
even smaller than a hummingbird.

552
00:34:55,600 --> 00:34:58,683
- Oh?
- Literally made of fire.

553
00:35:01,200 --> 00:35:02,565
It only lives for a minute.

554
00:35:02,680 --> 00:35:06,651
It blazes different colours...and sings.

555
00:35:08,400 --> 00:35:11,927
It gets so bright
you have to close your eyes.

556
00:35:13,960 --> 00:35:15,564
And when you open them, it's gone.

557
00:35:19,560 --> 00:35:23,246
But the image stays behind your eyelids
for longer than it was alive.

558
00:35:24,320 --> 00:35:25,481
Tell me another one.

559
00:35:25,600 --> 00:35:27,648
- I've said enough.
- No, go on, tell me.

560
00:35:27,760 --> 00:35:29,091
Just tell me about your life,

561
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:31,601
all the things that you've never said.

562
00:35:31,720 --> 00:35:33,722
How many children did you have, Jack?

563
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:36,366
I've lived a lot of lifetimes, Gwen,
I can't tell you everything.

564
00:35:36,480 --> 00:35:39,484
A lot of lifetimes.
That's a consolation, isn't it? Is it?

565
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:41,364
When you've had
more lives than anyone...

566
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,244
It's not enough.

567
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:49,051
- I don't want to die.
- I know.

568
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:53,970
I'm so sorry, Jack.

569
00:35:54,080 --> 00:35:55,605
It just...

570
00:35:55,720 --> 00:35:59,725
It went crazy, like...like bloodlust.

571
00:35:59,840 --> 00:36:00,841
I was so scared.

572
00:36:00,960 --> 00:36:03,440
Are you going to take the wrist strap?

573
00:36:04,720 --> 00:36:06,927
I'm a good thief.
I could have taken it any night.

574
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:08,644
You'd better clean up.

575
00:36:10,680 --> 00:36:12,523
We've got to go. Can you stand?

576
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:14,005
Give me a minute.

577
00:36:24,640 --> 00:36:27,086
I bought some inattention from Nico,

578
00:36:27,200 --> 00:36:29,328
the guy who's supposed to be
watching you,

579
00:36:29,440 --> 00:36:31,204
but it won't last for ever.

580
00:36:31,320 --> 00:36:32,731
You can put these on.

581
00:36:34,680 --> 00:36:35,966
Who were the three men?

582
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:38,646
What men?

583
00:36:38,760 --> 00:36:40,171
There were three men.

584
00:36:41,640 --> 00:36:43,642
Like they were making...

585
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:45,524
an agreement.

586
00:36:45,640 --> 00:36:47,927
I don't know. Hurry up.

587
00:36:56,240 --> 00:36:58,527
ANGELO: Hurry,
there's a train out tonight!

588
00:36:58,640 --> 00:37:00,404
Train where? Where are we going?

589
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:03,410
Like you said, we'll go to the West Coast,
Los Angeles, together.

590
00:37:07,240 --> 00:37:08,366
Jack!

591
00:37:12,680 --> 00:37:14,409
Jack!

592
00:37:16,680 --> 00:37:18,091
Where are you going?

593
00:37:18,200 --> 00:37:19,850
I left something here.

594
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:24,529
You left something in a vent on a roof?

595
00:37:25,640 --> 00:37:28,371
Ha! Never go far without it.

596
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:38,844
- OK, but now we go.
- I'm going, yeah.

597
00:37:38,960 --> 00:37:40,121
Time to move on.

598
00:37:41,960 --> 00:37:43,689
But not with you.

599
00:37:48,400 --> 00:37:49,526
I'm sorry.

600
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:54,727
I was terrified, Jack.
They said you were the devil,

601
00:37:54,840 --> 00:37:56,001
but other people said
you were a blessing...

602
00:37:56,120 --> 00:37:57,770
Something happened to me once,

603
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:59,803
a long way away.

604
00:37:59,920 --> 00:38:05,609
Time itself changed me
to a...fixed point. And now I can't die.

605
00:38:05,720 --> 00:38:08,485
I suffer and I perish...

606
00:38:10,040 --> 00:38:11,530
...but I always come back.

607
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:16,328
I've lived through a lot of Earth's past
and a lot of its future.

608
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:19,011
And I'll keep on
living this life for ever.

609
00:38:19,120 --> 00:38:21,487
- In the future, are we together?
- What does it matter?

610
00:38:21,600 --> 00:38:22,681
- Are we together?
- We can't be,

611
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:24,643
cos one day you're going to die

612
00:38:24,760 --> 00:38:26,569
- and I won't.
- Then we forget the future.

613
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:29,285
We make the moment now.

614
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:32,370
- We make a promise and we go forward.
- Angelo,

615
00:38:32,480 --> 00:38:35,086
- don't.
- What? You're lonely, too.

616
00:38:35,200 --> 00:38:36,486
You said you want a companion.

617
00:38:36,600 --> 00:38:38,409
- Don't make me do this.
- You're not going without me!

618
00:38:38,520 --> 00:38:40,602
- Just let me go.
- But you can't!

619
00:38:40,720 --> 00:38:41,960
I'm never going to let you go.

620
00:38:42,080 --> 00:38:44,481
I could travel this whole wide world,

621
00:38:44,600 --> 00:38:47,001
but where would I find
another man like you?

622
00:38:47,120 --> 00:38:51,045
Please, don't leave me on my own.

623
00:38:54,320 --> 00:38:55,731
I'm sorry, Angelo,

624
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:59,287
but this is the story of my life.

625
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:02,530
It always ends the same way.

626
00:39:05,560 --> 00:39:06,971
You kill me.

627
00:39:15,480 --> 00:39:16,925
Men like you...

628
00:39:19,360 --> 00:39:21,886
...you kill me.
- No!

629
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:30,084
No! No!

630
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:33,010
No! Jack!

631
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:10,646
- Know her?
- No.

632
00:40:10,760 --> 00:40:12,000
- OK.
- WOMAN: Thank you.

633
00:40:12,120 --> 00:40:16,364
You followed the instructions,
as far as I can tell.

634
00:40:16,480 --> 00:40:17,970
Captain Harkness,

635
00:40:18,080 --> 00:40:19,889
the last mortal man.

636
00:40:21,200 --> 00:40:23,202
It has been a long journey.

637
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:29,848
-
- What the hell?!

638
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:31,291
- Find out who that is!
- It's on you.

639
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:33,289
Who is it?

640
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:34,561
What the hell are they doing?!

641
00:40:37,800 --> 00:40:39,290
Gotcha.

642
00:40:39,400 --> 00:40:41,129
Bad day, Gwen?

643
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:00,124
- Rex.
- Yeah?

644
00:41:00,240 --> 00:41:02,402
Rex, you gotta see this.

645
00:41:02,520 --> 00:41:05,126
I was just checking the cache
on the I-5s. Look what it says.

646
00:41:05,240 --> 00:41:08,369
- Can we track them?
- Yes.

647
00:41:08,480 --> 00:41:09,845
Oh, Gwen!

648
00:41:09,960 --> 00:41:12,804
- You ready?
- I'm ready.

649
00:41:12,920 --> 00:41:14,684
Must be Rex and Esther.

650
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:16,689
- She's still got Anwen.
- Not for long.

651
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:20,287
Uh, you've got a little something
on you there.

652
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:24,246
Now unless you want to be
diagnosed Category 1...

653
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:26,560
Put your guns down.

654
00:41:28,960 --> 00:41:31,486
OK, get back! Get back! Back!

655
00:41:34,840 --> 00:41:36,842
- Her hands are up.
- Yes.

656
00:41:36,960 --> 00:41:39,088
Go, go, go!

657
00:41:40,520 --> 00:41:43,251
- All right, go, go, go!
-

658
00:41:44,400 --> 00:41:46,289
Grid one! Check him out!

659
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:48,607
One down. Living room clear.
Spread out, follow the grid.

660
00:41:48,720 --> 00:41:50,006
Yes, sir. Jackson, with me.

661
00:41:51,160 --> 00:41:53,811
Rhys, I can't believe it. We got you,
don't worry. You're all right.

662
00:41:53,920 --> 00:41:55,524
Took your bloody time!

663
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:57,529
Yes, I know, Mrs Cooper.
It's been frantic.

664
00:41:57,640 --> 00:41:58,766
We got this call. I was off duty...

665
00:41:58,880 --> 00:42:00,484
Gun. gun, gun!

666
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:06,885
I've never shot anyone before.

667
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:08,968
Where's Gwen?

668
00:42:09,080 --> 00:42:12,687
Andy! What's happened to Gwen?

669
00:42:19,280 --> 00:42:21,248
It's OK. It's OK.
Your family and baby, they're safe.

670
00:42:22,320 --> 00:42:25,244
Next time, just ask for help. I'm sick
of Torchwood acting like amateur clowns.

671
00:42:25,360 --> 00:42:27,124
Oh, you did it! Thank you!

672
00:42:27,240 --> 00:42:28,685
Got it?

673
00:42:28,800 --> 00:42:30,643
Thank you.
And you, you're going to live.

674
00:42:30,760 --> 00:42:31,921
It's a talent of mine.

675
00:42:32,040 --> 00:42:32,962
I meant every word I said.

676
00:42:33,080 --> 00:42:34,047
- So did I.
- Good.

677
00:42:34,160 --> 00:42:35,605
And as for you...

678
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:37,370
you'd better pray
that death comes back to this planet

679
00:42:37,480 --> 00:42:38,481
by the time I'm finished with you.

680
00:42:38,600 --> 00:42:41,206
So tell us who you are,
before I let her loose.

681
00:42:41,320 --> 00:42:44,802
I don't see that anything's changed.

682
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:46,365
You're still coming with me.

683
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:48,767
- Why would I do that?
- You'll want to come with me

684
00:42:48,880 --> 00:42:52,851
because I can take you to the one man
who knows how the miracle began.

685
00:42:52,960 --> 00:42:54,962
- Who's that?
- Angelo.

686
00:42:55,080 --> 00:42:58,004
Angelo Colasanto.

687
00:42:58,120 --> 00:43:00,009
He's waiting for you, Jack.

688
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:05,725
He's been waiting
for such a very long time.

689
00:43:12,760 --> 00:43:14,364
They don't exist.

690
00:43:16,320 --> 00:43:17,560
- Shit!
- What is it, Rex?

691
00:43:17,680 --> 00:43:19,569
Everybody, stay where you are!
Back down.

692
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:21,444
OK, OK, all right.

693
00:43:24,200 --> 00:43:26,328
- Leave me alone with him.
-

694
00:43:31,040 --> 00:43:33,520
- Goddamn it!
- Shit.

695
00:43:33,640 --> 00:43:35,881
While you were wasting time, Mr Shapiro,

696
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:37,331
we've got the names of the people
who are responsible

697
00:43:37,440 --> 00:43:40,569
for causing the miracle.
I suggest we get to work.

698
00:43:40,680 --> 00:43:43,331
He's preaching hellfire and salvation,
which makes Oswald Danes

699
00:43:43,440 --> 00:43:44,965
the most popular man in the world
right now.

700
00:43:46,080 --> 00:43:47,650
Get me a girl.

701
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:49,888
How old?

702
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:51,570
Mr Danes?

703
00:43:51,680 --> 00:43:55,127
I can act all kinds of innocent.

704
00:43:55,240 --> 00:43:56,162
Don't presume to know me.

705
00:43:56,280 --> 00:43:59,443
I am capable of far more
than my...reputation.

706
00:44:01,320 --> 00:44:03,800
I said...don't presume.

707
00:44:05,160 --> 00:44:08,801
Actually, if you don't mind,
I think I'd like to go.

708
00:44:08,920 --> 00:44:11,002
Don't! Don't you dare!

709
00:44:12,560 --> 00:44:15,040
This is like the whole world
is changing...

710
00:44:16,080 --> 00:44:18,003
...and we're just so tiny.

711
00:44:18,120 --> 00:44:20,009
There's a reason why Torchwood was secret.

712
00:44:20,120 --> 00:44:21,929
We kept things hidden from the human race.

713
00:44:22,040 --> 00:44:26,921
This technology is a science
the world should never know.

714
00:44:27,040 --> 00:44:28,963
This thing would be the end of us.
